Many people , including many Catholics , tend to mistake the Immaculate Conception for the conception of Jesus in Mary’s womb .
The Catholic Church professes that Mary was immaculately conceived – that by a special grace from God , she was “preserved free from all stain of original sin” from the first moment of her existence ( Pope Pius IX , Ineffabilis Deus ).
So , we see Mary as the New Eve and Ark of the New Covenant .
Could God have chosen a sinner to be the mother of His Son ?
But it was only appropriate that He chose the most-pure virgin .
Indeed , Mary’s holiness points directly to the holiness of her son , who was so holy that one can simply not imagine Him being made of sinful flesh .
It is true that the phrase , “Immaculate Conception , ” is not found in the Bible , and it is also true that the Bible nowhere states , “Mary was conceived without sin.” But then , the term “Holy Trinity” is not found in the Bible either .
However , the doctrine of the Immaculate Conception may be shown to be an authentic Biblical teaching .
