In our modern world, the English language should not be taught as a second language but as an indispensable tool for anyone who wants to communicate in a wide and diverse environment. For this purpose, from the first year of Nursery school, children receive hours of training in English.
English is taught as two hours a week in Nursery school and two hours and a half in Elementary.
Since 2018, the EFSR offers the possibility to certify the levels acquired in English and French.
Its mission is also to certify a student’s level in the French language. This is the A2 level of the DELF Prime, which is targeted at the end of CM2.
