Abstract:The article analyzes the original causes of internal discharge of 35kV indoor high-voltage switchgear in Lianzhou 35kV Xijiang Substation and proposes practical preventive measures, which are of positive significance to prevent such internal discharge of switchgear caused by moisture. Introduction
Qingyuan Lianzhou Power Supply Bureau has two 110kV substations and three 35kV substations using indoor high-voltage switchgear for 35kV voltage level equipment. In the past eight years, the 35kV indoor switchgear of the 1,000 substations were all affected by moisture.
Now the substation uses indoor type 35kv high-voltage cabinet, installs high-power heating and dehumidifying equipment at the bottom of the cabinet, and installs dehumidifiers, air conditioners and Shen cable trench blocking and other measures in the high-voltage room. Although the implementation of these measures to reduce the occurrence of accidents, but the equipment still has the following problems:
Stop by inspection found that the switch contact box and wear plate bushing surface had sticky and discharge traces caused by humidity (Figure 4). The above phenomenon shows that the safety hazard of 35kV switchgear still exists, and measures must be taken to eliminate the hidden danger.
If no measures are taken, in the rainy season weather, the switchgear operating environment is poor, the insulation performance of the insulation accessories inside the busbar room of the cabinet further decreases, which may occur in the phase discharge of high-voltage equipment, resulting in phase short-circuit fault, serious failure of the switchgear explosion, seriously affecting the safe operation of the equipment.
