Water filtration systems vary based on filter size, where they are installed, and how many taps in your home are treated. There are four basic types of water filter systems available:
Point of Use (POU) Systems — These more compact water filtration systems are installed underneath your kitchen sink to provide clean water for drinking and cooking from one tap. Most of ourreverse osmosis systemsfall under this category.
Pitcher Filters — these basic water filter systems can be bought in stores nationwide, and feature small carbon filters in a water pitcher that is refilled throughout the day and stored in the refrigerator.
Why buy a countertop water filtration system instead of an under-the-sink point of use system, or a more comprehensive point of entry system? Here are the top benefits of countertop systems:
Convenience — Looking for an effective yet easy solution for your water quality problems? Countertop water filters are the simplest water filtration systems to install, attaching directly to the tap.
