Even if there are risks, skin whitening is more popular than ever
These include special skin creams and laser treatments. Because of its low price and higher safety, many people choose skin creams.
Skin lightening basically refers to the use of special treatments or substances to improve or lighten skin tone. People use various terms to describe it, including whitening, lightening or whitening the skin.
People rely on whitening products and therapies to solve these problems. They use them to improve or restore skin tone.
Skin lightening is a global phenomenon, although there is reported greater interest in skin lightening in Africa, the Middle East and India. By 2013, it is predicted that by 2018, the global skin whitening product market will reach nearly 20 billion U.S. dollars.
Melanin is the main substance that plays a role in skin color. This is a type of dark polymer.
However, products that aim to achieve a fairer complexion often suffer from bad rap. According to reports, they cause various other problems that may make them not worth using at all.
People often use the term “bleaching” when talking about these safety issues. For this reason, companies usually avoid using it to describe their products.
We do not fully understand why some manufacturers choose this toxic ingredient. In view of the availability of safer or natural alternatives.
This is a very popular ingredient that manufacturers often include in recipes. Now, more and more people are aware of its dangers, which has led some companies to use clever descriptions for this, such as mercury, mercuric ammonia or mercury chloride.
Since then, many countries/regions (as early as the 1970s in Europe) have banned the use of this product to whiten skin. This substance is banned and classified as a toxin in the United States.
Except for vitiligo, doctors do not recommend the use of monobenzophenone under any other conditions. But you will be surprised to find that some companies include it in ordinary cosmetics.
Steroids may help whiten the skin in different ways. One of them is related to how they slow down the activity of melanocytes.
Steroids, including corticosteroids, are specifically used to treat inflammatory skin diseases. A prescription must also be issued, which means you’d better not find them in ordinary cosmetics.
However, people have been concerned about the ability of this ingredient to cause skin problems. Mineral oil can clog your skin pores, making it difficult to remove harmful substances.
