Is blow molding and blister molding all the same? Many people may have heard of these two, especially if you have ever worked in the packaging or printing industry, you must be familiar with both processes!
Blow molding process principle: use a split mold to inflate the plastic parison and close it to the inner wall of the mold. After cooling and demolding, various hollow products are obtained.
Blister packaging: the general term for using plastic blister technology to produce plastic products and encapsulating the products with corresponding equipment. In fact, the biggest difference between the two is that the blister process uses vacuum adsorption, while the blow molding is compressed air inflation molding, one is air extraction, and the other is air injection.
